\section{Introduction}
Valencian Sign Language (Llengua de signes valenciana, LSCV; ISO 639-3: vsv) is used by the deaf community of the Valencian Community in Spain. Several results mix it with Spanish Sign Language (LSE), so each item needs checking for which language it covers. No dedicated LSCV dictionary was found in this search.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item FESORD CV poster for the CNLSE congress 2022 on the legal status of sign language (Statute of Autonomy, art.\ 13.4) and a 2006 agreement with the education authority: \url{https://cnlse.es/es/actividades/congreso-cnlse-2022/programa-congreso-cnlse-2022/resumenes/poster_minguet.pdf}
\item FESORD CV summer activities document: \url{https://www.fesord.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/190531-Apunt-verano-1.pdf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia entry for the language; per its reference list, FESORD published the CD ``\textexclamdown A Signar!'' (1999) and the ``S\'igname'' course series (2000). Their current availability was not verified: \url{https://wikipedia.com/wiki/ISO_639:vsv}
\item UVdiscapacitat (Universitat de Val\`encia) SIGNA-UNI video vocabulary. It is LSE-based, validated by FESORD CV staff: \url{https://www.uv.es/uvdiscapacidad/es/recursos/software.html}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Fundaci\'on FESORD CV, created in 1998 as a reference centre for sign language in the Valencian Community. Its 2022 activity report: \url{https://www.fesord.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/MEMORIA-DE-ACTIVIDADES-2022_compressed-1.pdf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Information sheet for an introductory signs course at the Universitat Polit\`ecnica de Val\`encia: \url{https://casadelalumno.webs.upv.es/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/Informaci\%C3\%B3n_curso_signos.pdf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Legal commitments exist, but little school curriculum material specific to LSCV was found. FESORD CV is the natural partner for any curriculum work.
\end{document}
